  "result": "If I could change the world in one way, I\u2019d give every person a deeply rooted capacity for empathy\u2014an instinctive drive to understand and share others\u2019 experiences and perspectives. Imagine if, from early childhood onward, curiosity about someone else\u2019s story and a genuine desire to see life through their eyes were as natural as breathing. \n\nThat one shift\u2014widespread, automatic empathy\u2014would ripple outward:  \n\u2022 It would ease conflicts, because before blaming or dehumanizing \u201cthe other,\u201d people would instinctively ask, \u201cWhat pain or hope drives them?\u201d  \n\u2022 It would fuel cooperation on climate, health, and economic challenges, as we\u2019d feel personally invested in our neighbors\u2019 futures.  \n\u2022 It would make policies more humane, since leaders would be guided by an intimate sense of how decisions affect real lives.  \n\u2022 And it would transform daily interactions\u2014family fights, workplace tensions, strangers on the street\u2014into opportunities for connection rather than division.\n\nWith empathy built into our social fabric, distrust and indifference would shrink, and the collective will to solve global problems would grow stronger than any force pulling us apart.",
